de I'm  definitely not used to that but I could  see some people might think it's cool  now just looking at the layout of these  displays I like that the MacBook Pro  kinda has a full sheet of glass covering  the whole thing compared to the HP  having this kind of  old-style where the display is only on  the inside and you have like plastic  covering the whole exterior where the  bezels are at so definitely makes it  look old compared to the MacBook Pro  which I don't really like about it now  going down to the keyboards there's one  huge difference and that is the HP  choosing to add a numpad on the side so  they're using the full width compared to  the MacBook Pro which actually has some  pretty large speaker grilles on the  sides and they don't have the numpad and  of course the MacBook Pro has the touch  bar just like that so some people don't  like it I actually prefer the function  keys like you get on the HP getting into  the typing feel of the keyboard I really  like the MacBook Pros new magic keyboard  it gives you a lot more key travel than  before then the butterfly keys and some  good feedback as well now going over to  the omen I actually really like how much  key travel that you get of course is a  this is a thicker laptop so you get more  key travel and the feedback is also  really good it's a really tough choice  they feel pretty similar but yeah I  think the HP feels a little bit mushy  it's on the mushy side so I think I'd  actually go with the MacBook Pro for the  keyboard feel now if we move down to the  track pads this is where we see probably  the biggest difference ever so apples  track pads are known to be the best  because they use their force touch  technology so it doesn't actually click  it has a motor that vibrates and  assimilates a click so you can customize  all the different pressure settings and  the cool thing is that it doesn't use a  diving board design so anywhere you  click you get an even clicking feel  feels really great so b