ate but if you're gaming  it might not matter and as far as the  brightness the MacBook Pro is definitely  much more bright compared to the HP now  I have a video playing right here and  you can easily tell how much better the  colors the contrast everything is the  detail on the MacBook Pro compared to  the HP which really does not look that  great the colors just don't look nearly  as vibrant and everything has like a  blue tint to it because of the display  now let's go ahead and get into this  speaker comparison between these two  obviously the MacBook Pro costs over a  thousand dollars more so we should  expect the speakers to be better but I  notice on the  HP that there's Bang &amp; Olufsen speakers  so let's see how they sound so let me  know what you guys thought down in the  comment section below but that was a  massive difference  the MacBook Pro is better in literally  every single way the maids the wide  range of frequencies especially the bass  the volume now the speakers didn't sound  that bad on the omen except it was  lacking some bass and definitely  definitely lacking volume so the MacBook  Pro easily bit out the HP however the HP  omen should actually perform a lot  better than the 16 inch MacBook Pro so  let's get into the performance  comparison starting with Geekbench v now  these both have i7s their six cores but  the one in the omen has the brand-new  tenth generation one which we do expect  to be put into the sixteen inch macbook  pro hopefully sometime the summer so I  got the scores back and the performance  is a little bit underwhelming on the HP  4900 multi-core score compared to 5500  now the reason is because neither of  them are plugged in however I did check  the power settings and it's set to Best  Performance as you guys can see so you  have to be plugged in to get the full  performance so let's go ahead and plug  that in and retest this alright now that  is what I'm talking about check out that  single core score 1249 on the HP t